#Reflection from Part A

Through the concept analysis, I gained a better understanding of how Agentic Software Engineering 
extends the capabilities of traditional software systems. I learned that AI agents can do more than 
follow programmed instructions because they can interpret information, evaluate situations, and perform 
actions toward specific objectives. However, I also recognized that greater autonomy introduces 
additional responsibilities for developers.

The discussion also helped me understand why Agile development, Scrum, and 
version control are important when creating AI-powered applications. These practices allow developers 
to collaborate, identify problems, and continuously improve their systems. Most importantly, I realized 
that developing intelligent software is not only about making applications more efficient but also 
ensuring that they are safe, reliable, and ethical. Human supervision remains necessary because 
AI-generated decisions still require evaluation and accountability.

